    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5615054_40ff981b",
        "filename": "include/vboot.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-31T00:23:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently, we don\u0027t need to send a response in a packet. So, 0xec doesn\u0027t look needed except providing some hint for EC to detect data corruption.\n\nWhen we have a reverse packet (cr50-\u003eec), EC will have a packet parser. Then, the error codes will be transferred in a packet using the type field and we don\u0027t need to change enum cr50_comm_pd.",
      "parentUuid": "44a85f4b_b722ee36",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "fa18aa5e0354db25c3ab1ef69a2134bf13683992",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cbb15e04_819aa462",
        "filename": "include/vboot.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-31T18:20:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How are we going to transition from this \"raw\" mode to packet mode in the future? Can we just send back a packet now?\n\nI know this is more of a design point that we should determine, but both request and response should be packets with structure (even if it is a very simple structure)",
      "parentUuid": "f5615054_40ff981b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "fa18aa5e0354db25c3ab1ef69a2134bf13683992",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f4d7eb4_6ad1130e",
        "filename": "include/vboot.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-04T17:10:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If current EC receives a packet (as a response), the magic (0x4345) will be seen as invalid error code.\n\nIf future EC receives a raw error code, the error code will be seen as an invalid magic.\n\nIt\u0027s ok not to support features we don\u0027t use as long as there is a way to extend the protocol.",
      "parentUuid": "cbb15e04_819aa462",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "fa18aa5e0354db25c3ab1ef69a2134bf13683992",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
